==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|estraction|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|extractio|lang=la}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ækʃən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An act of [[extracting]] or the condition of being [[extracted]].
# A person's [[origin]] or [[ancestry]].
# Something extracted, an [[extract]], as from a [[plant]] or an organ of an animal etc.
# {{context|military|lang=en}} An act of removing someone from a hostile area to a secure location.
# {{context|dentistry|lang=en}} A removal of a [[tooth]] from its [[socket]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|origin, ancestry}} [[descent]], [[lineage]]

